  description="BirkyStudio vs Real Geeks honest comparison for real estate agents. Real Geeks charges $399/mo + $500 setup + lead packages, agents report trash leads and ignored support. BirkyStudio delivers verified prospects you own once, with AI follow-up."
  image="/images/comparison/realgeeks.jpg"
  >
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={faqLD} />
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={articleLD} />

    <!-- Hero -->
    <section style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#0f172a 0%,#1e1b4b 50%,#312e81 100%);padding:100px 0 80px;position:relative;overflow:hidden;">
    <div style="position:absolute;top:0;left:0;right:0;bottom:0;background:radial-gradient(circle at 20% 50%,rgba(99,102,241,0.15),transparent 50%),radial-gradient(circle at 80% 50%,rgba(236,72,153,0.1),transparent 50%);"></div>
    <div style="max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 32px;position:relative;z-index:1;">
      <div style="display:inline-block;padding:8px 20px;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.1);border-radius:100px;color:#a5b4fc;font-size:0.85rem;font-weight:500;margin-bottom:20px;">
        🔍 Updated September 2026 • Honest comparison
      </div>
      <h1 style="font-size:clamp(1.8rem,4vw,3rem);font-weight:800;color:white;margin-bottom:20px;line-height:1.15;">
        BirkyStudio vs Real Geeks<br>
        <span style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#818cf8,#f472b6);-webkit-background-clip:text;-webkit-text-fill-color:transparent;">"$2,400 Later and Not One Good Lead"</span>
      </h1>
      <p style="font-size:1.1rem;color:#cbd5e1;line-height:1.8;max-width:700px;">
        Real Geeks is a well-known real estate platform: a templated IDX website, a CRM, and managed paid-ad lead packages, all for a monthly fee plus a $500 setup charge. BirkyStudio takes a different route. We hand you a verified, enriched, scored list of real prospects you own forever, plus an AI that answers and qualifies the replies. One rents you a lead machine and a 12-month commitment. The other is a deliverable you keep. Here's the honest breakdown.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Main Content -->
  <section style="padding:80px 0;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#1a0f2e 0%,#2d1b4e 100%);">
    <div style="max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 32px;">

      <!-- Quick Answer -->
      <div style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#1e1b4b,#312e81);border-radius:16px;padding:32px;margin-bottom:64px;border:1px solid rgba(129,140,248,0.3);">
        <h2 style="color:white;font-size:1.3rem;margin-bottom:16px;">⚡ Quick Answer</h2>
        <p style="color:#cbd5e1;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:16px;">
          <strong style="color:white;">Choose BirkyStudio if:</strong> You want real, verified prospects delivered once and owned forever, with an AI that catches and qualifies replies the moment they come in. Best for solo agents and small teams tired of paying a monthly platform fee for leads they don't trust and don't own.<br><br>
          <strong style="color:white;">Choose Real Geeks if:</strong> You want a done-for-you IDX website plus managed paid-ad campaigns, you can commit to a 12-month term, and you have someone (or a team) ready to work the leads. Real Geeks' managed ad packages can genuinely scale for teams with a lead team behind them.<br><br>
          <strong style="color:white;">The honest difference:</strong> Real Geeks charges $399/month plus a $500 setup fee, requires a 12-month commitment for its lead packages, and can void your lead guarantee if you edit your own website. BirkyStudio charges once, hands you the prospects and the site, and lets you change anything.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Article Image 1 -->
      <div style="text-align:center;margin-bottom:64px;">
        <img src="/images/comparison/realgeeks-article-1.jpg" alt="Real estate agent reviewing a list of prospects on a laptop at a bright modern home office desk" style="width:100%;max-width:800px;border-radius:12px;height:auto;box-shadow:0 4px 24px rgba(0,0,0,0.3);" loading="lazy">
      </div>

      <!-- Why Compare -->
      <h2 style="font-size:1.6rem;font-weight:700;color:white;margin-bottom:16px;">Why compare BirkyStudio and Real Geeks?</h2>
      <p style="color:#cbd5e1;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:16px;">
        Real Geeks is one of the most established names in real estate lead generation. The pitch is appealing: they build you an IDX website, connect it to a CRM, and run paid advertising campaigns that deliver leads into your pipeline, social leads, search leads, and seller leads, depending on the package. It's marketed as "the best marketing and technology ROI in real estate," and for the right team, that can be true.
      </p>
      <p style="color:#cbd5e1;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:16px;">
        BirkyStudio competes on a different axis. Instead of renting you a lead machine on a monthly subscription, we deliver a finished product: a verified, enriched, scored list of real prospects for your niche and area. Every entry is checked for a working phone, email, and website, then enriched with data no lead platform provides, do they have a website? An AI agent? A chatbot? What tech are they running? What's their quality score? What do they need from you? You own it forever.
      </p>
      <p style="color:#cbd5e1;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:40px;">
        Both are trying to answer the same question: "how do I get more clients?" But they answer it differently, and the difference shows up in the price, in what you own, in what happens when you want out, and in what agents actually report after they've paid. That's what this page breaks down.
      </p>

      <!-- Comparison Table -->
      <h2 id="comparison" style="font-size:1.6rem;font-weight:700;color:white;margin-bottom:24px;">BirkyStudio vs Real Geeks. Side by Side</h2>
      <div style="overflow-x:auto;margin-bottom:64px;">
        <table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:0.9rem;">
