            </tr>
            <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);">
              <td style="padding:14px 12px;color:white;font-weight:600;">Website Included</td>
              <td style="padding:14px 12px;color:white;font-weight:600;">✅ $499 / $999 / $1,999, you own the code</td>
              <td style="padding:14px 12px;color:white;font-weight:600;">⚠️ Templated IDX site (editing it can void the lead guarantee)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);background:rgba(255,255,255,0.02);">
              <td style="padding:14px 12px;color:white;font-weight:600;">CRM Included</td>
              <td style="padding:14px 12px;color:white;font-weight:600;">✅ Notion Real Estate System (in $1,297 AI Agent Setup)</td>
              <td style="padding:14px 12px;color:white;font-weight:600;">✅ Built-in CRM, agents report it's laggy and lacks features</td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);">
              <td style="padding:14px 12px;color:white;font-weight:600;">Free Trial</td>
              <td style="padding:14px 12px;color:white;font-weight:600;">✅ 30-day money-back guarantee</td>
              <td style="padding:14px 12px;color:white;font-weight:600;">❌ No free trial</td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);background:rgba(255,255,255,0.02);">
              <td style="padding:14px 12px;color:white;font-weight:600;">Dedicated Support</td>
              <td style="padding:14px 12px;color:white;font-weight:600;">✅ Same person who built it</td>
              <td style="padding:14px 12px;color:white;font-weight:600;">⚠️ Ticket-based, users report slow, passive responses</td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);">
              <td style="padding:14px 12px;color:white;font-weight:600;">No Lock-In</td>
              <td style="padding:14px 12px;color:white;font-weight:600;">✅ No contract, no subscription</td>
              <td style="padding:14px 12px;color:white;font-weight:600;">❌ Subscription with term commitments</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <!-- Article Image 2 -->
      <div style="text-align:center;margin-bottom:64px;">
        <img src="/images/comparison/realgeeks-article-2.jpg" alt="Small real estate team collaborating around a table with laptops in a bright modern office" style="width:100%;max-width:800px;border-radius:12px;height:auto;box-shadow:0 4px 24px rgba(0,0,0,0.3);" loading="lazy">
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed Review: BirkyStudio -->
      <h2 style="font-size:1.6rem;font-weight:700;color:white;margin-bottom:32px;">Detailed Reviews</h2>

      <div id="birky-studio" style="background:rgba(129,140,248,0.08);border:1px solid rgba(129,140,248,0.3);border-radius:16px;padding:32px;margin-bottom:32px;">
        <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;margin-bottom:16px;">
          <span style="background:#818cf8;color:white;padding:4px 12px;border-radius:100px;font-size:0.75rem;font-weight:600;">YOU OWN IT</span>
          <h3 style="color:white;font-size:1.3rem;margin:0;">BirkyStudio</h3>
        </div>
        <p style="color:#cbd5e1;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:16px;">
          BirkyStudio's lead-generation offer starts with a Verified Prospect List: a real, enriched, scored list of prospects built for your niche and area. Every contact is checked for a working phone, email, and website, no bots, no recycled numbers, no "half the emails don't work." Then we enrich each one with detail no lead platform gives you: do they have a website? An AI agent? A chatbot? What tech stack? A 0-100 quality score? An "opportunity" tag that tells you exactly how to approach them.
        </p>
        <p style="color:#cbd5e1;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:16px;">
          You own the list forever. No subscription, no monthly platform fee, no $500 setup charge, no required ad budget, nothing to cancel. The Pipeline Bundle takes it further: it adds automated outreach, an AI agent trained on your niche and pitch, and an AI receptionist that catches and qualifies replies the moment they bite, on WhatsApp and phone, in English and Spanish. That's the closed loop Real Geeks never offers: not just the leads, but the follow-up machine that turns them into conversations.
        </p>
        <p style="color:#cbd5e1;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:16px;">
          Because it's one-time and fixed-cost, it works for agents at any level, and it's the direct answer to the agent who posted "$2,400 later… still not one good lead." One deal pays for it. And because you own everything, there's no lock-in and nothing to lose if you stop.
        </p>
        <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:24px;margin-bottom:16px;">
          <div>
            <p style="color:white;font-weight:600;font-size:0.9rem;margin-bottom:8px;">✅ Pros</p>
            <ul style="color:#cbd5e1;line-height:1.8;padding-left:20px;">
              <li>Verified, real prospects, not bots or dead numbers</li>
              <li>Enriched with website/tech/AI data and a 0-100 quality score</li>
              <li>You own the list and data forever</li>
              <li>One-time price, no setup fee, no contract, no ad budget</li>
              <li>AI agent + receptionist catch and qualify replies 24/7</li>
              <li>WhatsApp and bilingual (EN/ES) included</li>
              <li>Website you fully own and can edit ($499 / $999 / $1,999)</li>
              <li>Works for any niche, not just real estate</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p style="color:white;font-weight:600;font-size:0.9rem;margin-bottom:8px;">⚠️ Cons</p>
            <ul style="color:#cbd5e1;line-height:1.8;padding-left:20px;">
              <li>One-time deliverable, no built-in "fresh leads every month" ad engine</li>
              <li>List size is fixed by the tier you choose, not unlimited</li>
              <li>No managed paid-ad campaigns (you'd run those yourself)</li>
              <li>You may want a refresh for returning clients (offered at a discount)</li>
              <li>Smaller team, less brand recognition than an established platform</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p style="color:#818cf8;font-weight:600;">
          Pricing: Verified Prospect List $497 (Starter) / $997 (Pro) · Pipeline Bundle $1,997 (Pro List + outreach + AI Agent + AI receptionist, one integrated SKU) · AI Agent Setup $1,297 · Websites $499 / $999 / $1,999 · Optional Support &amp; Maintenance $197/month
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Article Image 3 -->
      <div style="text-align:center;margin-bottom:64px;">
        <img src="/images/comparison/realgeeks-article-3.jpg" alt="Real estate agent smiling while answering a phone call at a wooden desk with a laptop in warm light" style="width:100%;max-width:800px;border-radius:12px;height:auto;box-shadow:0 4px 24px rgba(0,0,0,0.3);" loading="lazy">
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed Review: Real Geeks -->
      <div id="realgeeks" style="background:rgba(255,255,255,0.03);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);border-radius:16px;padding:32px;margin-bottom:64px;">
        <h3 style="color:white;font-size:1.3rem;margin-bottom:16px;">Real Geeks</h3>
        <p style="color:#cbd5e1;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:16px;">
          Real Geeks is a long-established real estate marketing and technology platform. You get a templated IDX website, a built-in CRM, and optional managed lead packages: Social leads ($299/month per package), Search leads ($599/month per package), and Seller leads ($599/month per package). The base platform is $399/month with a one-time $500 setup fee, and the lead packages require a 12-month or 6-month commitment, with the 6-month term costing more per month. Geek AI Text runs $49/month (included free with any lead package).
        </p>
        <p style="color:#cbd5e1;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:16px;">
          When it works, the model is legitimate: Real Geeks runs your ads and you get leads flowing into a site and CRM they maintain. For a team with an ISA or a lead team behind them, that managed ad engine can genuinely scale. The company even publishes a lead guarantee, if they don't deliver the minimum guaranteed leads over your term, you get a one-month credit (12-month terms) or a half-month credit (6-month terms).
        </p>
        <p style="color:#cbd5e1;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:16px;">
          But read the fine print, and read the reviews. The lead guarantee is <em>invalidated</em> if you make changes to the code or content on the templated website they provided, including your home search pages, home valuation pages, and lead forms. In practice, improving your own website can void your guarantee. And the reviews are blunt: agents call the leads "trash," report that "half the phone numbers and emails don't work," describe the CRM as "laggy" and missing features, and one agent wrote that after three months and $2,400 they still hadn't gotten one good lead: "I feel totally ripped off." Support complaints are just as consistent, one agent described "begging them to fix my CRM since October and I have received a passive response."
        </p>
        <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:24px;margin-bottom:16px;">
          <div>
            <p style="color:white;font-weight:600;font-size:0.9rem;margin-bottom:8px;">✅ Pros</p>
